The HP are about what I usually have for wombats, the AC is a little
light (I usually want -25 or better for everyone) but not horrible.

Just a general comment: you have a lot of situations where I'd think
"that's kind of nasty" and then you follow it up with "I lost an
amulet of life saving here" or even 2 "oLS.  I don't think I've ever
used a "oLS during an ascension, and I've only triggered one 1-2 times
in a non-ascension.

Consider saving your !full healing instead of quaffing for a measly 8
hp; any time you're remotely in danger, have a couple in main
inventory and quaff whenever you're <100hp or otherwise in need.

I pretty much only quaff for max HP if I have enough that I'm sure I
have plenty and the weight of carrying is an issue (I'll quaff if I
have more than 10-15 of 'em).

Did you have conflict?  Jumping?  Both are more important than
another /death or whatever for the endgame, IMO.

Once I wake Rodney:
1. Always 1 !full healing in inv unless I'm so low on them that a
stray fire trap or whatever would be really bad.
2. Always wearing conflict
3. Always wearing jumping
4. Never levitating except when required--you can't jump while
levitating
5. Always a light source on
6. Always /digging, /teleport, /death, /cold, and /fire in main inv

